      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith a DFlash2 draft (candidate selector) or a LiLiCorr head, the draft sampler is folded into the draft CUDA graph. Its static buffers are sized to the largest captured decode bucket, but every decode step staged its sampling params into them. When a decode batch is larger than `--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode`, the scheduler crashes:\n\n```text\nFile \".../speculative/dflash_worker_v2.py\", line 293, in stage_sampling_params\n    self.greedy_mask[:bs].copy_(\nRuntimeError: The size of tensor a (4) must match the size of tensor b (8) at non-singleton dimension 0\n```\n\nThat step's draft cannot replay (no captured bucket covers the batch). It runs the eager head, which reads none of the sampler's buffers, so the staging is not needed.\n\nOur default Beam launch did not hit this: it ran 12 requests per rank and captured graphs up to 12. It happens when `--max-running-requests` exceeds the graph max or `--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode` is lowered. Under attention DP with #46837, it also happens when one rank's batch exceeds the graph max.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- `DFlashWorkerV2._stage_draft_sampler` stages the folded sampler only when the batch fits its buffers (`bs <= max_bs`).\n- `_SelectorDraftSampler` records its `max_bs`; `LiLiCorrDraftSampler` already does.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nBeam-1.0-501B-A23B-NVFP4 + Beam-1.0-501B-A23B-DFlash2 (block 8), 4x GB300, TP4, `trtllm_mha`, page 64, unified memory, `--cuda-graph-max-bs-decode 4`, 8 concurrent ShareGPT requests (512 output tokens, temperature 0):\n\n| | Result |\n|---|---|\n| main | Scheduler crash (the traceback above) |\n| this PR | 48/48 requests; accept length 3.45; no errors |\n\nUnder attention DP (TP4 / attention DP4 / EP4 FlashInfer MegaMoE) with #46837 applied, at the same graph max and about 4.5 requests per rank: crash without this change, 108/108 requests with it.\n\nThe GPU runs used main at `1f834c19` plus the MegaMoE autotune fix from #46213, which this image needs at startup. The change is the same as on this branch.\n\n- `test/registered/unit/spec/test_dflash*.py`: 62 passed, the same as on main.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot affected: this only skips host-side staging for steps whose draft cannot replay.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not needed: no flag or behavior change.\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #41364446552](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41364446552)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #41364446639](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41364446639)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #41364446564](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/41364446564)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n",
